    "evidence_text": "Empirical Bayesian models for analysing molecular serotyping microarrays\n\nRESULTS We propose an empirical Bayesian model for calculating the probabilities of combinations of serotypes from the microarray data.\n\nThe model also enabled the presence of combinations of serotypes within samples to be determined.\n\nPrecision microbiome reconstitution restores bile acid mediated resistance to Clostridium difficile\n\nMany antibiotics destroy intestinal microbial communities and increase susceptibility to intestinal pathogens.\n\nIMPORTANCE Identification of the bacterium responsible for an outbreak can aid in disease management.\n\nRESULTS During phase 1, a draft genome of the STEC outbreak strain was obtained.\n\nMETHODS AND FINDINGS Reference sample sets were distributed to 15 research groups for blinded testing.\n\nThe major limitation of this study is that not all of the available alternative serotyping methods were included.   \n\n\nMicroarray with a culture amplification step was the top-performing method.\n\nBacterial vaccines can reduce carriage rates.\n\nColonization is usually a binary endpoint.\n\nIn general, detection by qPCR and culture was consistent.\n\nHuman papillomavirus genotype 31 does not express detectable microRNA levels during latent or productive virus replication.\n\nMicroarray analysis of pneumococcal gene expression during invasive disease.\n\ntested.",
